# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own writing `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wconversion"`, the group above it, before
# `#include <stdlib.h>` turned the build's `-Werror=sign-conversion` off for
# every line the compiler wrote after it, and `abs(x: u32)` against C's
# `int abs(int)` built and printed `5`; through a header that only includes
# `<stdlib.h>` it is refused `ffi_parameter_type`.
#
# CAUSE: a pragma outranks the command line for the rest of the unit, and
# the probe that checks the parameter stands after the header.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-ignoring-wconversion-turns-off-no-check.h"
    function abs(x: u32) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(abs(5))
